Subject: [PATCH 1/5] src/lab-process-mail: Answer the inbox from outside the
 tree
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: ukpzutoumtvxkskmvvonmrmpwzxtkkxv

The process-email loop ran from a Justfile in the trunk workspace,
which is the same tree the agent edits. When a pass moved that
workspace to a commit without the recipes, the loop could no longer
find its own notify and get-up-to-date steps, and it died after
answering a message. Any loop that reads its own code from the tree
under edit can break this way, or quietly change between passes.

lab-process-mail is a standalone tool meant to run from an installed
copy, outside the tree. The deterministic work stays in the script: it
fetches, rebases trunk work and the outbox, picks the oldest inbox
message, runs claude on it, checks the inbox afterwards, and posts to
ntfy. Everything that needs judgement is in prompt.md, which ships
beside the script, so a pass cannot edit the instructions it runs
under either.

The prompt takes one named message and does not loop, so the script
alone decides which message each pass is for and can verify that
exactly that message was answered.
